@title From Register Sale to Online Stock Count
@subtitle A guide for new engineers
@author Retail Platform team
@date 2026-10-08

!! The Stock Ledger is the only source of truth for stock. The Storefront count may lag by up to 20 seconds.

## Sale-to-stock sequence

diagram sale sequence title="A sale reaches the online stock count"
sale: pos "Store POS" svc
sale: agent "Edge Sync Agent" svc
sale: api "Inventory API" svc
sale: ledger "Stock Ledger" db
sale: store "Storefront" ext
sale: pos -> agent : sale recorded, 2 units of SKU 48113
sale: agent -> api : POST /adjustments, batched every 5 seconds
sale: api -> ledger : append decrement
sale: ledger --> api : new on-hand count
sale: api --> agent : 202 Accepted
sale: api -> store : publish stock change
sale: note agent : when the store link is down, adjustments wait in a local queue
sale: opt "store connection restored"
sale: agent -> api : replay queued adjustments
sale: end

When the store loses its connection, Store POS keeps selling. Edge Sync Agent keeps the adjustments in a local queue, then sends them in order when the link returns.

## Timing budget

table = Hop,Limit; Register to agent,under 1 second; Agent batch interval,5 seconds; API to ledger,under 200 milliseconds; Ledger to storefront,under 10 seconds; **End to end**,**under 20 seconds for 99% of sales**

## Good to know

- The local queue holds up to 4 hours of sales, about 3000 adjustments at a busy store.
- Adjustments carry an idempotency key, so replays never double count.
- Online orders reserve stock for 15 minutes at checkout.
